<para id="RM000001Z2Q00BX" category="D" type-id="304JI" name-id="480XS-00" from="200612">
<name>Freeze Frame Data</name>
<subpara id="RM000001Z2Q00BX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AZU00000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<step1>
<ptxt>Freeze Frame Data</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When a malfunction DTC is output, the freeze frame data at the time the malfunction code was set is stored.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Once the freeze frame data at the time a malfunction DTC was set has been stored, the data is not updated or erased until the stored data is cleared (DTCs cleared).</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<step2>
<ptxt>Turn IG OFF.</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Display the malfunction codes on the DTC code check screen. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000URU00GX"/>)</ptxt>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Select a code displaying "F" (freeze data present) and check the freeze frame data.</ptxt>
